{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014gmdK85ro2cUJ4Wyhx9EGL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Insights from Negative Results in NLP EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Call for Main Conference Papers - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/calls/main_conference_papers/\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"CFP | Insights 2024\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2021/cfp/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Insights 2024 | Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=883\"},{\"title\":\"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/proceedings/10.5555/1613715\"},{\"title\":\"2026 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Call For Papers: The Second Workshop on Insights from Negative Results (EMNLP 2021) | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/call-papers-second-workshop-insights-negative-results-emnlp-2021-0\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about EMNLP 2026's approach to negative results and related reviewer guidelines:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 and Negative Results\n\nEMNLP 2026 has a goal of curating a diverse technical program that includes negative findings, survey papers, new resources, position papers, novel linguistic insights using existing computational techniques, and reproduction or failure to reproduce previous results.\n\n## Related Reviewer Guidelines\n\nThe search results include information about general ARR (ACL Rolling Review) reviewer guidelines and EMNLP's approach to peer review. ARR developed detailed guidelines and suggestions for each step of the reviewing process, including a list of common problems in both reviews and NLP papers to watch out for.\n\n## Workshop on Insights from Negative Results\n\nThere is also a separate workshop series dedicated to this topic. Publication of negative results is difficult in most fields, but in NLP the problem is exacerbated by the near-universal focus on improvements in benchmarks, which implicitly discourages hypothesis-driven research and turns model creation and fine-tuning into art rather than science. The workshop invites practical and theoretical unexpected or negative results that have important implications for future research, highlight methodological issues with existing approaches, and/or point out pervasive misunderstandings or bad practices.\n\nUnfortunately, I could not locate a specific EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form specifically for \"Insights from Negative Results\" papers in the search results. The information above reflects EMNLP 2026's general openness to negative results and related reviewing infrastructure.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73f9f140-4f70-4f54-821d-08400ec577d5","uuid":"c673d1a2-8c19-4577-b4af-0027799fbf76","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:45:54.689Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Insights from Negative Results in NLP EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01EywGD44LU4EQB7kG39hLzT","content":[{"title":"Call for Main Conference Papers - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/calls/main_conference_papers/"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"CFP | Insights 2024","url":"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2021/cfp/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Insights 2024 | Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP","url":"https://insights-workshop.github.io/"},{"title":"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing 2027 2026 2025 ...","url":"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=883"},{"title":"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/"},{"title":"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/proceedings/10.5555/1613715"},{"title":"2026 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Call For Papers: The Second Workshop on Insights from Negative Results (EMNLP 2021) | ACL Member Portal","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/call-papers-second-workshop-insights-negative-results-emnlp-2021-0"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about EMNLP 2026's approach to negative results and related reviewer guidelines:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 and Negative Results\n\nEMNLP 2026 has a goal of curating a diverse technical program that includes negative findings, survey papers, new resources, position papers, novel linguistic insights using existing computational techniques, and reproduction or failure to reproduce previous results.\n\n## Related Reviewer Guidelines\n\nThe search results include information about general ARR (ACL Rolling Review) reviewer guidelines and EMNLP's approach to peer review. ARR developed detailed guidelines and suggestions for each step of the reviewing process, including a list of common problems in both reviews and NLP papers to watch out for.\n\n## Workshop on Insights from Negative Results\n\nThere is also a separate workshop series dedicated to this topic. Publication of negative results is difficult in most fields, but in NLP the problem is exacerbated by the near-universal focus on improvements in benchmarks, which implicitly discourages hypothesis-driven research and turns model creation and fine-tuning into art rather than science. The workshop invites practical and theoretical unexpected or negative results that have important implications for future research, highlight methodological issues with existing approaches, and/or point out pervasive misunderstandings or bad practices.\n\nUnfortunately, I could not locate a specific EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form specifically for \"Insights from Negative Results\" papers in the search results. The information above reflects EMNLP 2026's general openness to negative results and related reviewing infrastructure."],"durationSeconds":5.691990926000003}}
