llingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"ACL ARR | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about the ACL Rolling Review scoring system:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. Additionally, the soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\nHowever, the search results did not provide the specific scoring scale values (such as the numerical range or detailed descriptions for each score level) for the soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation scores. To get more detailed information about the specific scoring scale, you may want to check the ACL Rolling Review Review Form directly at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform or consult the detailed reviewer guidelines."],"durationSeconds":4.500124194000003}}
