{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TgrTiBF4yqeVvv7e6tWwZw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform soundness excitement overall assessment scale 1 2 3 4 5\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Policies - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-acl23/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/\"},{\"title\":\"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2026 on X: \\\"Checkout the blog post on the soundness/excitement scores https://t.co/AKSO9DjiYP . It clarifies the reasoning behind the separation of overall scores and how it might make the reviewer recommendation more robust. #ACL2023Toronto #ACL2023NLP #NLProc\\\" / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/aclmeeting/status/1637827267173953540\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found from the ACL Rolling Review website regarding the soundness, excitement, and overall assessment scales:\n\n## Soundness Scale\n\nThe soundness scale includes: 5 = Excellent (this study is one of the most thorough), 4 = Strong (provides sufficient support for all claims, though some extra experiments could be nice), and 3 = Acceptable (provides sufficient support for main claims).\n\n## Excitement Scale\n\nFor excitement: 5 = Highly Exciting (would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation), and 4 = Exciting (would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation).\n\n## Overall Assessment Scale\n\nThe overall assessment scale includes: 5 = Consider for Award (could be considered for an outstanding paper award at an *ACL conference), 2 = Resubmit next cycle (needs substantial revisions by the next ARR cycle), 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle (needs substantial revisions that cannot be completed by next cycle), and 1 = Do not resubmit (paper must be fully redone or is not relevant to the *ACL community).\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73f9f140-4f70-4f54-821d-08400ec577d5","uuid":"895d6c4b-a5d0-402f-8e53-c6d6beaca64f","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:46:34.033Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform soundness excitement overall assessment scale 1 2 3 4 5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_016ap6BUFoWyzNWdiVBTTWKz","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Policies - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-acl23/"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/"},{"title":"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf"},{"title":"ACL 2026 on X: \"Checkout the blog post on the soundness/excitement scores https://t.co/AKSO9DjiYP . It clarifies the reasoning behind the separation of overall scores and how it might make the reviewer recommendation more robust. #ACL2023Toronto #ACL2023NLP #NLProc\" / X","url":"https://x.com/aclmeeting/status/1637827267173953540"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found from the ACL Rolling Review website regarding the soundness, excitement, and overall assessment scales:\n\n## Soundness Scale\n\nThe soundness scale includes: 5 = Excellent (this study is one of the most thorough), 4 = Strong (provides sufficient support for all claims, though some extra experiments could be nice), and 3 = Acceptable (provides sufficient support for main claims).\n\n## Excitement Scale\n\nFor excitement: 5 = Highly Exciting (would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation), and 4 = Exciting (would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation).\n\n## Overall Assessment Scale\n\nThe overall assessment scale includes: 5 = Consider for Award (could be considered for an outstanding paper award at an *ACL conference), 2 = Resubmit next cycle (needs substantial revisions by the next ARR cycle), 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle (needs substantial revisions that cannot be completed by next cycle), and 1 = Do not resubmit (paper must be fully redone or is not relevant to the *ACL community).\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation."],"durationSeconds":6.265321889999999}}
