{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TgFnx8cUJ15BBmwxfXGvg3","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_2/projects/tax_error_inject_agent/memory.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Memory — tax_error_inject_agent\\\\n\\\\n## 关键发现\\\\n\\\\n- **v4 正式判定: Gate 3a FAIL, Gate 3b FAIL**: TaxEI 61.7% = vanilla 61.7%, random 66.0% 反超。Taxonomy 标签在 clean-task eval 上无额外价值。所有 McNemar 检验无显著性（n=47, discordant=10）。\\\\n- **Recovery eval 同样 FAIL**: TaxEI 59.6% ≤ Vanilla 61.7%，head-to-head gained 4 lost 5 net -1。Taxonomy 标签在 recovery 场景也无系统性优势。\\\\n- **Detection rate 全 0%**: 所有模型（vanilla/taxei/random）detection_rate=0。当前 eval 框架只检查最终任务成功，没有机制捕捉\\\\\\\"模型是否意识到错误发生\\\\\\\"。Detection 指标在当前框架下无意义——这是 eval 设计局限，不是模型能力结论。\\\\n- **C4 observation_masking 是 TaxEI 唯一正向 operator (+9.1pp)**: 暗示 taxonomy 标签可能只在信息缺失类错误上有微弱价值，但在 step 重排/删除类错误上反而有害。这个 pattern 值得在 negative paper 中讨论。\\\\n- **TaxEI 训练方差 3.3× vanilla** (SD=10.5pp vs 3.2pp): 注入导致训练极不稳定。这本身就是 negative finding——即使平均效果为零，高方差也意味着不可靠。\\\\n- **D012 \\\\\\\"系统性损害\\\\\\\" 结论 premature**: 方法差异与 seed 高度交互（seed=42 注入≈vanilla，seed=0 注入大幅下降）。不是稳定主效应，而是 noise-dominated。这对 paper framing 重要——不能说 \\\\\\\"systematically harms\\\\\\\"，应说 \\\\\\\"does not reliably improve and increases variance\\\\\\\"。\\\\n- **统计功效严重不足**: n=47 的 McNemar 需要 ~17pp 才有 power，而观察效应 (11pp 均值差) 与跨 seed 噪声 (10-15pp) 在同一量级。补充实验需要更多 seed 或更大 eval set。\\\\n- **TaxEI pick_two_obj 严重退化**: 28.6% vs vanilla/random 57.1%，完全抵消其他维度的微弱优势。\\\\n- **v3 vs v4 趋势不一致**: v3 vanilla>taxei>random, v4 random>taxei=vanilla。说明 v3 数据不平衡确实是混淆变量。\\\\n- **格式对齐修复有效**: v3-vanilla SFT 74.5% vs baseline 42.6%，+31.9pp。v1 的 14.9% 崩溃是训练/eval 格式不匹配。\\\\n- **GPT-5.2 ALFWorld 成功率 ~70%** (501/714)。\\\\n- **TaxEI v1 的\\\\\\\"保护效应\\\\\\\"是假象**: build_recovery_prompt() 恰好用了类似 eval 的格式。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] permutation test bug 修复后所有比较不显著**: `multiseed_stats.py` 有浮点精度 bug（`mean(a)-mean(b)` vs `mean(a-b)` 差 ~1e-17，边界情况导致 p=0）。修复后 TaxEI vs Vanilla pooled p=0.017→**0.054 (NS)**，TaxEI vs Random p=0.051→0.170 (NS)。paper_framing 中 \\\\\\\"p=0.03\\\\\\\" 需更正。Narrative 应从 \\\\\\\"significant degradation\\\\\\\" 改为 \\\\\\\"directional but not statistically significant\\\\\\\"。修复方法: (1) `diff_obs` 改用 `np.mean(diffs)` 统一计算路径 (2) p 值改 `(count+1)/(n_perm+1)` 避免 p=0（Phipson & Smyth 2010）。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Random 3-seed 完整: 63.1% ± 6.8pp**: seed=42 66.0%, seed=0 55.3%, seed=123 68.1%。排序: Vanilla (65.3%) > Random (63.1%) > TaxEI (56.7%)，但所有 pairwise 均不显著。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Dose-response baseline 修正**: 所有 dose-response 实验 seed=42，应对比 vanilla seed=42 (61.7%) 非 3-seed 均值 (65.3%)。修正后: 10% injection → 0pp（非 -3.6pp），25% injection → -12.8pp（非 -16.4pp）。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] TaxEI dose-response 呈阈值效应**: 0%→61.7%, 10%→61.7%(0pp), 25%→48.9%(-12.8pp), 50%→51.1%(-10.6pp)。25% 最差而非 50%。曲线在 ~15-20% 处存在 critical threshold——低于阈值无影响，高于阈值产生退化但不再持续恶化（plateau）。之前 R²=0.961 的线性拟合是两点假象。与 noise-ratio threshold 理论 (Rolnick 2017, Ye et al. ICLR 2025) 一致。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Random 10% 注入反而提升性能 (+6.4pp)**: Random 10% = 68.1% vs vanilla seed=42 61.7%。TaxEI 10% = 61.7% (0pp)。在低注入比例下，随机错误注入起到数据增强作用（增加轨迹多样性），而 taxonomy 标签限制了错误分布的多样性导致无效果。这是 TaxEI vs Random 的关键差异化证据——taxonomy 标签不仅无益，在低比例时还不如随机注入。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Training dynamics 悖论: 注入改善训练但恶化 eval**: 50% injection (taxei/random) final loss 0.26 vs vanilla 0.29, max acc 0.93 vs 0.91——训练指标全面优于 vanilla。但 eval: taxei 50%=51.1%, vanilla=61.7%。模型 overfit 到注入数据的分布（包括错误模式），train loss 下降反映的是对这些模式的记忆，而非对 clean task 的泛化。这对 paper 重要：可以论证 injection 不是简单的\\\\\\\"加噪声\\\\\\\"——模型确实学到了注入内容，只是学到的内容有害。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Training-eval mismatch 文献解释链**: Error injection → 训练分布偏移 (Longpre 2020) → 模型先学 clean pattern 再 memorize noise (Arpit 2017, Liu 2020) → SFT loss 优化的是 surface-level 拟合而非 downstream capability (Zhou 2023 LIMA) → 偏移的训练分布加剧 catastrophic forgetting，覆写预训练知识 (Luo 2023)。Injection 比例越高，链条每个环节都放大，导致 50% injection \\\\\\\"训练最好、eval 最差\\\\\\\"。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] ⚠️ \\\\\\\"恒定 6.4pp taxonomy penalty\\\\\\\" 是离散化伪迹**: Per-task cross-analysis (art_20260515_d1414a) 确认：三个 dose 点（10%/25%/50%）中 TaxEI 失败但 Random 成功的 task 几乎完全不同。全部 3 个 dose 出现的 penalty task = **0 个**。2/3 出现 = 4 个（且分属不同 dose 对）。涉及的 penalty task 总计 9 个不同 task。47-task 粒度下分辨率 ≈ 2.13pp/task，Δ=3 tasks ≈ 6.4pp 是巧合，不是系统性惩罚。**Paper 中不能 claim \\\\\\\"constant additive taxonomy penalty\\\\\\\"**——应改为\\\\\\\"stochastic penalty that happens to average ~3 tasks per evaluation\\\\\\\"。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Per-task 3-seed 平均的 taxonomy gap 仍有参考价值**: pick_cool (-19pp) 和 pick_two (-14pp) 的 3-seed 平均 gap 可能反映 task-type 层面的趋势（需更多 seed 确认），但 dose-response 内的 per-task 翻转是随机的。两个层面的分析不矛盾：3-seed 看 task-type 趋势，dose-response 看 individual task 翻转。\\\\n\\\\n## 文献调研关键洞察 (2026-05-14)\\\\n\\\\n- **PALADIN 数字已验证**: 32.76% → 89.68% RR (Gemma-3-12B) 准确。但 PALADIN 不是纯 SFT — 包含 inference-time retrieval (55+ exemplars)，去掉 retrieval 后 RR 降 ~30pp。当前 paper_framing 未充分讨论此 confound。\\\\n- **PALADIN 没有多 seed 验证**: 只用 bootstrap N=1000 做统计检验，无跨 random seed variance。我们的多 seed 设计反而是方法论贡献。\\\\n- **PALADIN 用 80/20 ratio at 50K scale**: 比我们的 50/50 at 9K 更激进但规模大 5.5×。injection ratio × scale 的交互是关键未解问题。\\\\n- **ALFWorld SOTA**: CoEx 93.28% (EMNLP Findings 2025), AgentPRM 91.0% (2025), Reflexion+GPT-4 ~97% (multi-trial)。我们的 65.3% 在 SFT-only 8B 范畴合理。\\\\n- **EEF (arXiv 2504.13145) 是重要对比**: 从失败中提取好 signal 而非注入坏 signal，在 WebShop 上成功。这是关键 contrast — injection 方向可能根本错误。\\\\n- **AgentDebug (arXiv 2509.25370) 有 ALFWorld error taxonomy**: 5 维 (memory/reflection/planning/action/system)，比我们的 4 operators 更全面但方法论不同 (debugging vs augmentation)。\\\\n- **除 PALADIN 外无其他 taxonomy-guided error injection 工作** — 我们是第一个跨域迁移尝试。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Dose-response 文献定位**: 无先前工作报告 agent SFT 中直接错误注入的 dose-response 曲线。现有方法用 contrastive/DPO (ETO) 或配对 recovery 演示 (PALADIN)，回避了直接混入。我们的 10%→25% 阈值是该设定下首个实证锚点。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Training-eval mismatch 有 4 层文献支撑**: (1) memorization dynamics (Arpit 2017, Liu 2020), (2) superficial alignment hypothesis (Zhou 2023 LIMA), (3) catastrophic forgetting from distribution shift (Luo 2023), (4) augmentation failure modes (Longpre 2020)。这些论文为 negative paper Discussion 提供了强理论框架。\\\\n\\\\n## 设计决策\\\\n\\\\n- **D004 RandomInjector**: 使用与 TaxEI 完全相同的 4 个算子，唯一区别是 `[Error Type: P1_xxx]` → `[Error occurred]`。\\\\n- **D005/D006 v4 同源方案**: 同一份 760 条 injected_variants 格式化两次，TaxEI=Random=9,029 samples，唯一变量是 error tag 文本。\\\\n- **D009/D010 Option C (Recovery Eval + 多种子验证)**: Gate FAIL 不可撤回。Recovery eval 是补充分析（非替代 Gate）。\\\\n- **D014 项目转向**: 全维度否定后转 negative result paper。对标 PALADIN (tool-use 正面) vs TaxEI (embodied planning 负面)。\\\\n- **核心对比维度 (negative paper)**: embodied planning (ALFWorld, long-horizon, spatial) vs tool-use (ToolBench, API call, discrete)。Error injection 可能只在 action space 离散且可枚举的场景有效。\\\\n- **Fixed-size ablation 设计**: 总量固定 4,358（= vanilla 大小），变量只是 injection ratio (10%/25%/50%)。数据在 `data/mini_pipeline_v4/ablation_fixed/` 目录下已预生成。\\\\n\\\\n## 约束\\\\n\\\\n- **submit_training_job 的 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES 不可靠**: tmux wrapper 不一定正确传递环境变量。**必须**在 command 字符串中显式前置 `export CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=N &&`（放在 swift 命令之前，同一 shell）。仅靠 gpu 参数不够。[2026-05-14 事故: inject25 r1 因此 OOM]\\\\n- **submit_training_job 必须 bash -c 包装**: tmux 用 sh，不包装会 EXIT_CODE=127。\\\\n- **eval 参数: `--device cuda:0`（不是 `--gpu 0`）**。\\\\n- **checkpoint 查找必须用 `sort -V`**: `ls -dt .../v0-*/ | head -1` 选最新 run，`ls -d checkpoint-* | sort -V | tail -1` 选最大 step。不要硬编码路径。\\\\n- **轨迹收集**: `export TMPDIR=/root/autodl-tmp/tmp` 防 /tmp 满。已完成 501 条。\\\\n- **SIGHUP 误杀**: Worker 执行 `tmux kill-session` 前必须先确认进程异常。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Dose-response baseline**: 所有 dose-response ablation 用 seed=42，对比 vanilla seed=42 (61.7%)，不用 3-seed 均值。\\\\n\\\\n## 模型版本\\\\n\\\\n- **ms-swift**: 4.2.0\\\\n- **Qwen3-8B**: /root/autodl-tmp/models/Qwen/Qwen3-8B\\\\n- **GPT-5.2**: trajectory collection + recovery demo generation\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 7150, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73f9f140-4f70-4f54-821d-08400ec577d5","uuid":"1a0adece-354a-47e0-b040-d6f11e0d2d97","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:52:47.898Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_2/projects/tax_error_inject_agent/memory.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Memory — tax_error_inject_agent\\\\n\\\\n## 关键发现\\\\n\\\\n- **v4 正式判定: Gate 3a FAIL, Gate 3b FAIL**: TaxEI 61.7% = vanilla 61.7%, random 66.0% 反超。Taxonomy 标签在 clean-task eval 上无额外价值。所有 McNemar 检验无显著性（n=47, discordant=10）。\\\\n- **Recovery eval 同样 FAIL**: TaxEI 59.6% ≤ Vanilla 61.7%，head-to-head gained 4 lost 5 net -1。Taxonomy 标签在 recovery 场景也无系统性优势。\\\\n- **Detection rate 全 0%**: 所有模型（vanilla/taxei/random）detection_rate=0。当前 eval 框架只检查最终任务成功，没有机制捕捉\\\\\\\"模型是否意识到错误发生\\\\\\\"。Detection 指标在当前框架下无意义——这是 eval 设计局限，不是模型能力结论。\\\\n- **C4 observation_masking 是 TaxEI 唯一正向 operator (+9.1pp)**: 暗示 taxonomy 标签可能只在信息缺失类错误上有微弱价值，但在 step 重排/删除类错误上反而有害。这个 pattern 值得在 negative paper 中讨论。\\\\n- **TaxEI 训练方差 3.3× vanilla** (SD=10.5pp vs 3.2pp): 注入导致训练极不稳定。这本身就是 negative finding——即使平均效果为零，高方差也意味着不可靠。\\\\n- **D012 \\\\\\\"系统性损害\\\\\\\" 结论 premature**: 方法差异与 seed 高度交互（seed=42 注入≈vanilla，seed=0 注入大幅下降）。不是稳定主效应，而是 noise-dominated。这对 paper framing 重要——不能说 \\\\\\\"systematically harms\\\\\\\"，应说 \\\\\\\"does not reliably improve and increases variance\\\\\\\"。\\\\n- **统计功效严重不足**: n=47 的 McNemar 需要 ~17pp 才有 power，而观察效应 (11pp 均值差) 与跨 seed 噪声 (10-15pp) 在同一量级。补充实验需要更多 seed 或更大 eval set。\\\\n- **TaxEI pick_two_obj 严重退化**: 28.6% vs vanilla/random 57.1%，完全抵消其他维度的微弱优势。\\\\n- **v3 vs v4 趋势不一致**: v3 vanilla>taxei>random, v4 random>taxei=vanilla。说明 v3 数据不平衡确实是混淆变量。\\\\n- **格式对齐修复有效**: v3-vanilla SFT 74.5% vs baseline 42.6%，+31.9pp。v1 的 14.9% 崩溃是训练/eval 格式不匹配。\\\\n- **GPT-5.2 ALFWorld 成功率 ~70%** (501/714)。\\\\n- **TaxEI v1 的\\\\\\\"保护效应\\\\\\\"是假象**: build_recovery_prompt() 恰好用了类似 eval 的格式。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] permutation test bug 修复后所有比较不显著**: `multiseed_stats.py` 有浮点精度 bug（`mean(a)-mean(b)` vs `mean(a-b)` 差 ~1e-17，边界情况导致 p=0）。修复后 TaxEI vs Vanilla pooled p=0.017→**0.054 (NS)**，TaxEI vs Random p=0.051→0.170 (NS)。paper_framing 中 \\\\\\\"p=0.03\\\\\\\" 需更正。Narrative 应从 \\\\\\\"significant degradation\\\\\\\" 改为 \\\\\\\"directional but not statistically significant\\\\\\\"。修复方法: (1) `diff_obs` 改用 `np.mean(diffs)` 统一计算路径 (2) p 值改 `(count+1)/(n_perm+1)` 避免 p=0（Phipson & Smyth 2010）。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Random 3-seed 完整: 63.1% ± 6.8pp**: seed=42 66.0%, seed=0 55.3%, seed=123 68.1%。排序: Vanilla (65.3%) > Random (63.1%) > TaxEI (56.7%)，但所有 pairwise 均不显著。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Dose-response baseline 修正**: 所有 dose-response 实验 seed=42，应对比 vanilla seed=42 (61.7%) 非 3-seed 均值 (65.3%)。修正后: 10% injection → 0pp（非 -3.6pp），25% injection → -12.8pp（非 -16.4pp）。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] TaxEI dose-response 呈阈值效应**: 0%→61.7%, 10%→61.7%(0pp), 25%→48.9%(-12.8pp), 50%→51.1%(-10.6pp)。25% 最差而非 50%。曲线在 ~15-20% 处存在 critical threshold——低于阈值无影响，高于阈值产生退化但不再持续恶化（plateau）。之前 R²=0.961 的线性拟合是两点假象。与 noise-ratio threshold 理论 (Rolnick 2017, Ye et al. ICLR 2025) 一致。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Random 10% 注入反而提升性能 (+6.4pp)**: Random 10% = 68.1% vs vanilla seed=42 61.7%。TaxEI 10% = 61.7% (0pp)。在低注入比例下，随机错误注入起到数据增强作用（增加轨迹多样性），而 taxonomy 标签限制了错误分布的多样性导致无效果。这是 TaxEI vs Random 的关键差异化证据——taxonomy 标签不仅无益，在低比例时还不如随机注入。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Training dynamics 悖论: 注入改善训练但恶化 eval**: 50% injection (taxei/random) final loss 0.26 vs vanilla 0.29, max acc 0.93 vs 0.91——训练指标全面优于 vanilla。但 eval: taxei 50%=51.1%, vanilla=61.7%。模型 overfit 到注入数据的分布（包括错误模式），train loss 下降反映的是对这些模式的记忆，而非对 clean task 的泛化。这对 paper 重要：可以论证 injection 不是简单的\\\\\\\"加噪声\\\\\\\"——模型确实学到了注入内容，只是学到的内容有害。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Training-eval mismatch 文献解释链**: Error injection → 训练分布偏移 (Longpre 2020) → 模型先学 clean pattern 再 memorize noise (Arpit 2017, Liu 2020) → SFT loss 优化的是 surface-level 拟合而非 downstream capability (Zhou 2023 LIMA) → 偏移的训练分布加剧 catastrophic forgetting，覆写预训练知识 (Luo 2023)。Injection 比例越高，链条每个环节都放大，导致 50% injection \\\\\\\"训练最好、eval 最差\\\\\\\"。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] ⚠️ \\\\\\\"恒定 6.4pp taxonomy penalty\\\\\\\" 是离散化伪迹**: Per-task cross-analysis (art_20260515_d1414a) 确认：三个 dose 点（10%/25%/50%）中 TaxEI 失败但 Random 成功的 task 几乎完全不同。全部 3 个 dose 出现的 penalty task = **0 个**。2/3 出现 = 4 个（且分属不同 dose 对）。涉及的 penalty task 总计 9 个不同 task。47-task 粒度下分辨率 ≈ 2.13pp/task，Δ=3 tasks ≈ 6.4pp 是巧合，不是系统性惩罚。**Paper 中不能 claim \\\\\\\"constant additive taxonomy penalty\\\\\\\"**——应改为\\\\\\\"stochastic penalty that happens to average ~3 tasks per evaluation\\\\\\\"。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Per-task 3-seed 平均的 taxonomy gap 仍有参考价值**: pick_cool (-19pp) 和 pick_two (-14pp) 的 3-seed 平均 gap 可能反映 task-type 层面的趋势（需更多 seed 确认），但 dose-response 内的 per-task 翻转是随机的。两个层面的分析不矛盾：3-seed 看 task-type 趋势，dose-response 看 individual task 翻转。\\\\n\\\\n## 文献调研关键洞察 (2026-05-14)\\\\n\\\\n- **PALADIN 数字已验证**: 32.76% → 89.68% RR (Gemma-3-12B) 准确。但 PALADIN 不是纯 SFT — 包含 inference-time retrieval (55+ exemplars)，去掉 retrieval 后 RR 降 ~30pp。当前 paper_framing 未充分讨论此 confound。\\\\n- **PALADIN 没有多 seed 验证**: 只用 bootstrap N=1000 做统计检验，无跨 random seed variance。我们的多 seed 设计反而是方法论贡献。\\\\n- **PALADIN 用 80/20 ratio at 50K scale**: 比我们的 50/50 at 9K 更激进但规模大 5.5×。injection ratio × scale 的交互是关键未解问题。\\\\n- **ALFWorld SOTA**: CoEx 93.28% (EMNLP Findings 2025), AgentPRM 91.0% (2025), Reflexion+GPT-4 ~97% (multi-trial)。我们的 65.3% 在 SFT-only 8B 范畴合理。\\\\n- **EEF (arXiv 2504.13145) 是重要对比**: 从失败中提取好 signal 而非注入坏 signal，在 WebShop 上成功。这是关键 contrast — injection 方向可能根本错误。\\\\n- **AgentDebug (arXiv 2509.25370) 有 ALFWorld error taxonomy**: 5 维 (memory/reflection/planning/action/system)，比我们的 4 operators 更全面但方法论不同 (debugging vs augmentation)。\\\\n- **除 PALADIN 外无其他 taxonomy-guided error injection 工作** — 我们是第一个跨域迁移尝试。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Dose-response 文献定位**: 无先前工作报告 agent SFT 中直接错误注入的 dose-response 曲线。现有方法用 contrastive/DPO (ETO) 或配对 recovery 演示 (PALADIN)，回避了直接混入。我们的 10%→25% 阈值是该设定下首个实证锚点。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Training-eval mismatch 有 4 层文献支撑**: (1) memorization dynamics (Arpit 2017, Liu 2020), (2) superficial alignment hypothesis (Zhou 2023 LIMA), (3) catastrophic forgetting from distribution shift (Luo 2023), (4) augmentation failure modes (Longpre 2020)。这些论文为 negative paper Discussion 提供了强理论框架。\\\\n\\\\n## 设计决策\\\\n\\\\n- **D004 RandomInjector**: 使用与 TaxEI 完全相同的 4 个算子，唯一区别是 `[Error Type: P1_xxx]` → `[Error occurred]`。\\\\n- **D005/D006 v4 同源方案**: 同一份 760 条 injected_variants 格式化两次，TaxEI=Random=9,029 samples，唯一变量是 error tag 文本。\\\\n- **D009/D010 Option C (Recovery Eval + 多种子验证)**: Gate FAIL 不可撤回。Recovery eval 是补充分析（非替代 Gate）。\\\\n- **D014 项目转向**: 全维度否定后转 negative result paper。对标 PALADIN (tool-use 正面) vs TaxEI (embodied planning 负面)。\\\\n- **核心对比维度 (negative paper)**: embodied planning (ALFWorld, long-horizon, spatial) vs tool-use (ToolBench, API call, discrete)。Error injection 可能只在 action space 离散且可枚举的场景有效。\\\\n- **Fixed-size ablation 设计**: 总量固定 4,358（= vanilla 大小），变量只是 injection ratio (10%/25%/50%)。数据在 `data/mini_pipeline_v4/ablation_fixed/` 目录下已预生成。\\\\n\\\\n## 约束\\\\n\\\\n- **submit_training_job 的 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES 不可靠**: tmux wrapper 不一定正确传递环境变量。**必须**在 command 字符串中显式前置 `export CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=N &&`（放在 swift 命令之前，同一 shell）。仅靠 gpu 参数不够。[2026-05-14 事故: inject25 r1 因此 OOM]\\\\n- **submit_training_job 必须 bash -c 包装**: tmux 用 sh，不包装会 EXIT_CODE=127。\\\\n- **eval 参数: `--device cuda:0`（不是 `--gpu 0`）**。\\\\n- **checkpoint 查找必须用 `sort -V`**: `ls -dt .../v0-*/ | head -1` 选最新 run，`ls -d checkpoint-* | sort -V | tail -1` 选最大 step。不要硬编码路径。\\\\n- **轨迹收集**: `export TMPDIR=/root/autodl-tmp/tmp` 防 /tmp 满。已完成 501 条。\\\\n- **SIGHUP 误杀**: Worker 执行 `tmux kill-session` 前必须先确认进程异常。\\\\n- **[2026-05-15] Dose-response baseline**: 所有 dose-response ablation 用 seed=42，对比 vanilla seed=42 (61.7%)，不用 3-seed 均值。\\\\n\\\\n## 模型版本\\\\n\\\\n- **ms-swift**: 4.2.0\\\\n- **Qwen3-8B**: /root/autodl-tmp/models/Qwen/Qwen3-8B\\\\n- **GPT-5.2**: trajectory collection + recovery demo generation\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 7150, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}","structuredContent":{"result":"{\"success\": true, \"data\": {\"path\": \"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_2/projects/tax_error_inject_agent/memory.md\", \"content\": \"# Memory — tax_error_inject_agent\\n\\n## 关键发现\\n\\n- **v4 正式判定: Gate 3a FAIL, Gate 3b FAIL**: TaxEI 61.7% = vanilla 61.7%, random 66.0% 反超。Taxonomy 标签在 clean-task eval 上无额外价值。所有 McNemar 检验无显著性（n=47, discordant=10）。\\n- **Recovery eval 同样 FAIL**: TaxEI 59.6% ≤ Vanilla 61.7%，head-to-head gained 4 lost 5 net -1。Taxonomy 标签在 recovery 场景也无系统性优势。\\n- **Detection rate 全 0%**: 所有模型（vanilla/taxei/random）detection_rate=0。当前 eval 框架只检查最终任务成功，没有机制捕捉\\\"模型是否意识到错误发生\\\"。Detection 指标在当前框架下无意义——这是 eval 设计局限，不是模型能力结论。\\n- **C4 observation_masking 是 TaxEI 唯一正向 operator (+9.1pp)**: 暗示 taxonomy 标签可能只在信息缺失类错误上有微弱价值，但在 step 重排/删除类错误上反而有害。这个 pattern 值得在 negative paper 中讨论。\\n- **TaxEI 训练方差 3.3× vanilla** (SD=10.5pp vs 3.2pp): 注入导致训练极不稳定。这本身就是 negative finding——即使平均效果为零，高方差也意味着不可靠。\\n- **D012 \\\"系统性损害\\\" 结论 premature**: 方法差异与 seed 高度交互（seed=42 注入≈vanilla，seed=0 注入大幅下降）。不是稳定主效应，而是 noise-dominated。这对 paper framing 重要——不能说 \\\"systematically harms\\\"，应说 \\\"does not reliably improve and increases variance\\\"。\\n- **统计功效严重不足**: n=47 的 McNemar 需要 ~17pp 才有 power，而观察效应 (11pp 均值差) 与跨 seed 噪声 (10-15pp) 在同一量级。补充实验需要更多 seed 或更大 eval set。\\n- **TaxEI pick_two_obj 严重退化**: 28.6% vs vanilla/random 57.1%，完全抵消其他维度的微弱优势。\\n- **v3 vs v4 趋势不一致**: v3 vanilla>taxei>random, v4 random>taxei=vanilla。说明 v3 数据不平衡确实是混淆变量。\\n- **格式对齐修复有效**: v3-vanilla SFT 74.5% vs baseline 42.6%，+31.9pp。v1 的 14.9% 崩溃是训练/eval 格式不匹配。\\n- **GPT-5.2 ALFWorld 成功率 ~70%** (501/714)。\\n- **TaxEI v1 的\\\"保护效应\\\"是假象**: build_recovery_prompt() 恰好用了类似 eval 的格式。\\n- **[2026-05-15] permutation test bug 修复后所有比较不显著**: `multiseed_stats.py` 有浮点精度 bug（`mean(a)-mean(b)` vs `mean(a-b)` 差 ~1e-17，边界情况导致 p=0）。修复后 TaxEI vs Vanilla pooled p=0.017→**0.054 (NS)**，TaxEI vs Random p=0.051→0.170 (NS)。paper_framing 中 \\\"p=0.03\\\" 需更正。Narrative 应从 \\\"significant degradation\\\" 改为 \\\"directional but not statistically significant\\\"。修复方法: (1) `diff_obs` 改用 `np.mean(diffs)` 统一计算路径 (2) p 值改 `(count+1)/(n_perm+1)` 避免 p=0（Phipson & Smyth 2010）。\\n- **[2026-05-15] Random 3-seed 完整: 63.1% ± 6.8pp**: seed=42 66.0%, seed=0 55.3%, seed=123 68.1%。排序: Vanilla (65.3%) > Random (63.1%) > TaxEI (56.7%)，但所有 pairwise 均不显著。\\n- **[2026-05-15] Dose-response baseline 修正**: 所有 dose-response 实验 seed=42，应对比 vanilla seed=42 (61.7%) 非 3-seed 均值 (65.3%)。修正后: 10% injection → 0pp（非 -3.6pp），25% injection → -12.8pp（非 -16.4pp）。\\n- **[2026-05-15] TaxEI dose-response 呈阈值效应**: 0%→61.7%, 10%→61.7%(0pp), 25%→48.9%(-12.8pp), 50%→51.1%(-10.6pp)。25% 最差而非 50%。曲线在 ~15-20% 处存在 critical threshold——低于阈值无影响，高于阈值产生退化但不再持续恶化（plateau）。之前 R²=0.961 的线性拟合是两点假象。与 noise-ratio threshold 理论 (Rolnick 2017, Ye et al. ICLR 2025) 一致。\\n- **[2026-05-15] Random 10% 注入反而提升性能 (+6.4pp)**: Random 10% = 68.1% vs vanilla seed=42 61.7%。TaxEI 10% = 61.7% (0pp)。在低注入比例下，随机错误注入起到数据增强作用（增加轨迹多样性），而 taxonomy 标签限制了错误分布的多样性导致无效果。这是 TaxEI vs Random 的关键差异化证据——taxonomy 标签不仅无益，在低比例时还不如随机注入。\\n- **[2026-05-15] Training dynamics 悖论: 注入改善训练但恶化 eval**: 50% injection (taxei/random) final loss 0.26 vs vanilla 0.29, max acc 0.93 vs 0.91——训练指标全面优于 vanilla。但 eval: taxei 50%=51.1%, vanilla=61.7%。模型 overfit 到注入数据的分布（包括错误模式），train loss 下降反映的是对这些模式的记忆，而非对 clean task 的泛化。这对 paper 重要：可以论证 injection 不是简单的\\\"加噪声\\\"——模型确实学到了注入内容，只是学到的内容有害。\\n- **[2026-05-15] Training-eval mismatch 文献解释链**: Error injection → 训练分布偏移 (Longpre 2020) → 模型先学 clean pattern 再 memorize noise (Arpit 2017, Liu 2020) → SFT loss 优化的是 surface-level 拟合而非 downstream capability (Zhou 2023 LIMA) → 偏移的训练分布加剧 catastrophic forgetting，覆写预训练知识 (Luo 2023)。Injection 比例越高，链条每个环节都放大，导致 50% injection \\\"训练最好、eval 最差\\\"。\\n- **[2026-05-15] ⚠️ \\\"恒定 6.4pp taxonomy penalty\\\" 是离散化伪迹**: Per-task cross-analysis (art_20260515_d1414a) 确认：三个 dose 点（10%/25%/50%）中 TaxEI 失败但 Random 成功的 task 几乎完全不同。全部 3 个 dose 出现的 penalty task = **0 个**。2/3 出现 = 4 个（且分属不同 dose 对）。涉及的 penalty task 总计 9 个不同 task。47-task 粒度下分辨率 ≈ 2.13pp/task，Δ=3 tasks ≈ 6.4pp 是巧合，不是系统性惩罚。**Paper 中不能 claim \\\"constant additive taxonomy penalty\\\"**——应改为\\\"stochastic penalty that happens to average ~3 tasks per evaluation\\\"。\\n- **[2026-05-15] Per-task 3-seed 平均的 taxonomy gap 仍有参考价值**: pick_cool (-19pp) 和 pick_two (-14pp) 的 3-seed 平均 gap 可能反映 task-type 层面的趋势（需更多 seed 确认），但 dose-response 内的 per-task 翻转是随机的。两个层面的分析不矛盾：3-seed 看 task-type 趋势，dose-response 看 individual task 翻转。\\n\\n## 文献调研关键洞察 (2026-05-14)\\n\\n- **PALADIN 数字已验证**: 32.76% → 89.68% RR (Gemma-3-12B) 准确。但 PALADIN 不是纯 SFT — 包含 inference-time retrieval (55+ exemplars)，去掉 retrieval 后 RR 降 ~30pp。当前 paper_framing 未充分讨论此 confound。\\n- **PALADIN 没有多 seed 验证**: 只用 bootstrap N=1000 做统计检验，无跨 random seed variance。我们的多 seed 设计反而是方法论贡献。\\n- **PALADIN 用 80/20 ratio at 50K scale**: 比我们的 50/50 at 9K 更激进但规模大 5.5×。injection ratio × scale 的交互是关键未解问题。\\n- **ALFWorld SOTA**: CoEx 93.28% (EMNLP Findings 2025), AgentPRM 91.0% (2025), Reflexion+GPT-4 ~97% (multi-trial)。我们的 65.3% 在 SFT-only 8B 范畴合理。\\n- **EEF (arXiv 2504.13145) 是重要对比**: 从失败中提取好 signal 而非注入坏 signal，在 WebShop 上成功。这是关键 contrast — injection 方向可能根本错误。\\n- **AgentDebug (arXiv 2509.25370) 有 ALFWorld error taxonomy**: 5 维 (memory/reflection/planning/action/system)，比我们的 4 operators 更全面但方法论不同 (debugging vs augmentation)。\\n- **除 PALADIN 外无其他 taxonomy-guided error injection 工作** — 我们是第一个跨域迁移尝试。\\n- **[2026-05-15] Dose-response 文献定位**: 无先前工作报告 agent SFT 中直接错误注入的 dose-response 曲线。现有方法用 contrastive/DPO (ETO) 或配对 recovery 演示 (PALADIN)，回避了直接混入。我们的 10%→25% 阈值是该设定下首个实证锚点。\\n- **[2026-05-15] Training-eval mismatch 有 4 层文献支撑**: (1) memorization dynamics (Arpit 2017, Liu 2020), (2) superficial alignment hypothesis (Zhou 2023 LIMA), (3) catastrophic forgetting from distribution shift (Luo 2023), (4) augmentation failure modes (Longpre 2020)。这些论文为 negative paper Discussion 提供了强理论框架。\\n\\n## 设计决策\\n\\n- **D004 RandomInjector**: 使用与 TaxEI 完全相同的 4 个算子，唯一区别是 `[Error Type: P1_xxx]` → `[Error occurred]`。\\n- **D005/D006 v4 同源方案**: 同一份 760 条 injected_variants 格式化两次，TaxEI=Random=9,029 samples，唯一变量是 error tag 文本。\\n- **D009/D010 Option C (Recovery Eval + 多种子验证)**: Gate FAIL 不可撤回。Recovery eval 是补充分析（非替代 Gate）。\\n- **D014 项目转向**: 全维度否定后转 negative result paper。对标 PALADIN (tool-use 正面) vs TaxEI (embodied planning 负面)。\\n- **核心对比维度 (negative paper)**: embodied planning (ALFWorld, long-horizon, spatial) vs tool-use (ToolBench, API call, discrete)。Error injection 可能只在 action space 离散且可枚举的场景有效。\\n- **Fixed-size ablation 设计**: 总量固定 4,358（= vanilla 大小），变量只是 injection ratio (10%/25%/50%)。数据在 `data/mini_pipeline_v4/ablation_fixed/` 目录下已预生成。\\n\\n## 约束\\n\\n- **submit_training_job 的 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES 不可靠**: tmux wrapper 不一定正确传递环境变量。**必须**在 command 字符串中显式前置 `export CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=N &&`（放在 swift 命令之前，同一 shell）。仅靠 gpu 参数不够。[2026-05-14 事故: inject25 r1 因此 OOM]\\n- **submit_training_job 必须 bash -c 包装**: tmux 用 sh，不包装会 EXIT_CODE=127。\\n- **eval 参数: `--device cuda:0`（不是 `--gpu 0`）**。\\n- **checkpoint 查找必须用 `sort -V`**: `ls -dt .../v0-*/ | head -1` 选最新 run，`ls -d checkpoint-* | sort -V | tail -1` 选最大 step。不要硬编码路径。\\n- **轨迹收集**: `export TMPDIR=/root/autodl-tmp/tmp` 防 /tmp 满。已完成 501 条。\\n- **SIGHUP 误杀**: Worker 执行 `tmux kill-session` 前必须先确认进程异常。\\n- **[2026-05-15] Dose-response baseline**: 所有 dose-response ablation 用 seed=42，对比 vanilla seed=42 (61.7%)，不用 3-seed 均值。\\n\\n## 模型版本\\n\\n- **ms-swift**: 4.2.0\\n- **Qwen3-8B**: /root/autodl-tmp/models/Qwen/Qwen3-8B\\n- **GPT-5.2**: trajectory collection + recovery demo generation\\n\", \"total_chars\": 7150, \"truncated\": false}, \"error\": null, \"metadata\": {}}"}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XCmtZL8ATQ9pa34v5CUnqo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full picture. The memory confirms several critical issues:\n\n1. **Table 1 discrepancy**: The actual 3-seed results are:\n   - Vanilla: 61.7/68.1/66.0 → Mean=65.3, SD=3.3\n   - TaxEI: seed0 gave 46.8 or something? Actually memory says \"TaxEI 61.7% = vanilla 61.7%, random 66.0% 反超\" for seed 42. Then from the 3-seed data: Vanilla 65.3%, TaxEI 56.7%, Random 63.1%. \n\nLooking at the complete seed breakdown, I can see Vanilla had seeds 42, 0, and 123 producing 61.7%, 68.1%, and 66.0% respectively, while TaxEI's mean of 56.7% shows it underperformed across the board, with notably higher variance than vanilla's 3.3 percentage point spread.\n\nBut when I check Table 1 in the paper, those exact numbers—TaxEI at 64.5% mean and Random at 70.9%—match the dose=10% imagined experiment data from the config file, not the actual core results. The paper seems to have accidentally used the wrong dataset for its main table.\n\nThe 6.4 percentage point taxonomy penalty is looking like a discretization artifact based on what I'm seeing in the memory notes.\n\nThere's also the permutation test issue: the original p-value of 0.03 doesn't hold up after fixing the bug—it becomes 0.054, which isn't significant. The paper's \"updated\" pooled p-value of 0.031 has independence problems that make it unreliable.\n\nWebShop and the scale experiments are listed as imagined experiments in the config, and I'm not finding any actual results for them in the memory file, which suggests they may never have been run.\n\nLooking at what both reviewers flagged, there's clear agreement on the major issues: the Table 1 discrepancy, the taxonomy penalty being an artifact, and the statistical test having non-independence problems.\n\nBoth reviewers also converge on the same scores—Soundness 2, Excitement 3, Overall 2.5—and they both recognize that the per-operator locality gradient is genuinely the paper's strongest contribution. The core problem is data integrity, but they both see potential for acceptance with revisions.\n\nNow I'm ready to write the consolidated review.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4535,"cache_read_input_tokens":77573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4535},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73f9f140-4f70-4f54-821d-08400ec577d5","uuid":"2a575bb0-b41b-4b3b-83d9-057aeb3172f7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XCmtZL8ATQ9pa34v5CUnqo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've verified the key issues against the project memory. The memory confirms:\n1. **Actual 3-seed data**: Vanilla=65.3%±3.3, TaxEI=56.7% (SD~10.5pp), Random=63.1%±6.8pp — Table 1 shows completely different numbers\n2. **6.4pp claim explicitly flagged as artifact**: \"Paper 中不能 claim 'constant additive taxonomy penalty'\" \n3. **Permutation test bug**: corrected from p=0.03 to p=0.054 (NS)\n\nNow I'll compile the roundtable synthesis and submit.\n\n## Roundtable Step 2: Cross-Sharing\n\nBoth reviewers independently converged on the same critical issues:\n- **Table 1 data mismatch** (both MAJOR): Table 1 numbers match the dose=10% imagined experiment, not the actual core results\n- **6.4pp artifact** (both MAJOR): project memory explicitly warns against this claim\n- **Statistical inflation** (both flagged): pooled N=423 from non-independent observations\n- **Unverifiable experiments** (R2 MAJOR): WebShop, scale ablation appear only in \"imagined_experiments\"\n\n## Roundtable Step 3: Convergence\n\nFull agreement on scores (Soundness 2, Excitement 3, Overall 2.5) and on all four major issues. R1 provided deeper statistical critique; R2 provided broader related work gaps. Both agree the per-operator locality gradient is the paper's best contribution.\n\n## Roundtable Step 4: Final Consolidated Report"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4535,"cache_read_input_tokens":77573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4535},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73f9f140-4f70-4f54-821d-08400ec577d5","uuid":"d8d3571a-a272-45df-8400-9012aff5aa84"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XCmtZL8ATQ9pa34v5CUnqo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012QMXXxaPdU7wpm3M5EtpFy","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__submit_dream_review_report","input":{"report":"# Dream Review Report — Full Mode\n\n**Paper**: \"Error Injection Helps Tool-Use but Hurts Planning: Boundary Conditions for Failure-Augmented Agent Training\"\n**Venue**: Insights from Negative Results in NLP @ EMNLP 2026\n**Review Mode**: Full (2 Reviewers + Roundtable)\n**Scoring Framework**: ARR (Soundness/Excitement/Overall, 1–5 scale)\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThe paper tests whether taxonomy-guided error injection (successful in tool-use via PALADIN's +57pp on ToolBench) transfers to embodied planning (ALFWorld). Using a 4-operator error taxonomy and training Qwen3-8B under Vanilla/TaxEI/Random conditions, the authors report a negative result: TaxEI degrades performance and increases variance. Dose-response experiments, training dynamics analysis, qualitative failure analysis, WebShop replication, scale ablation, few-shot recovery, and per-operator analysis are presented. The paper concludes that error injection requires discrete, observable, locally recoverable errors to be effective.\n\nThe research question is timely and well-motivated. However, both reviewers independently identified serious data integrity issues that preclude acceptance in the current form.\n\n---\n\n## Consolidated Strengths\n\n1. **Well-suited for the venue.** This is a textbook negative-result paper: plausible hypothesis, rigorous experimental design, honest pivot to characterizing why the method fails. The Insights workshop values exactly this.\n\n2. **Per-operator locality gradient is the paper's strongest contribution.** The monotonic C4(+6.1pp) → P1(−2.7pp) → C1(−5.6pp) → P2(−8.4pp) relationship along error locality is conceptually elegant, bridges the macro tool-use/planning divide with micro within-environment evidence, and provides concrete actionable guidance.\n\n3. **Variance as primary finding is well-argued.** The observation that the primary effect is 2.6× variance increase (not just mean degradation) is practically important and methodologically novel. The F-test (p=0.038) for variance ratio is the most credible statistical result in the paper.\n\n4. **Controlled experimental design.** TaxEI and Random share identical injected trajectories with only the error tag text differing—an elegant isolation of the taxonomy-guidance variable. The fixed-size dose-response protocol (total=4,358) cleanly controls for data volume confounds.\n\n5. **Dose-response decomposition is novel.** No prior work varies injection ratio at fixed data size to isolate threshold effects in agent SFT. The finding that both methods collapse by ~12pp between 10–25% injection is potentially broadly applicable.\n\n6. **Multi-seed design is itself a contribution.** The paper demonstrates that single-seed evaluation of error injection is unreliable, which is actionable advice for the community—especially since PALADIN reports no multi-seed validation.\n\n---\n\n## Consolidated Weaknesses\n\n### MAJOR Issues\n\n**M1. Table 1 contains incorrect data that contradicts the abstract and all other results.**\n\nTable 1 reports: Vanilla=65.3±3.3, Random=70.9±3.3, TaxEI=64.5±3.3. The abstract reports: Vanilla=65.3%, TaxEI=56.7% (SD=8.6pp). The project's actual 3-seed data (confirmed in memory.md) is: Vanilla=65.3±3.3, TaxEI=56.7% (SD≈8.6–10.5pp), Random=63.1±6.8pp.\n\nCritically, Table 1 shows all three methods with identical SD=3.3pp, which directly contradicts the paper's central claim of a variance gradient (3.3 < 7.0 < 8.6). Yet the text below Table 1 asserts \"Vanilla SD (3.3pp) < Random SD (7.0pp) < TaxEI SD (8.6pp).\"\n\nThe Table 1 numbers (TaxEI: 61.7/68.1/63.8; Random: 68.1/74.5/70.2) exactly match the **dose=10% imagined experiment** from the review_context.yaml, not the actual core experiment. This appears to be a generation error where the dream report populated Table 1 with the wrong data source.\n\n**Severity**: Disqualifying until corrected. The paper's central table is wrong.\n\n**M2. The \"constant ~6.4pp taxonomy penalty\" is a known discretization artifact.**\n\nThe project's own per-task analysis (documented in memory.md) explicitly states: \"三个 dose 点中 TaxEI 失败但 Random 成功的 task 几乎完全不同。全部 3 个 dose 出现的 penalty task = 0 个\" and \"Paper 中不能 claim 'constant additive taxonomy penalty'——应改为'stochastic penalty that happens to average ~3 tasks per evaluation'.\"\n\nWith 47 binary tasks, resolution is ~2.13pp/task. Δ=3 tasks ≈ 6.4pp. The near-perfect constancy across 9 seed×dose cells (Table 3: 8 cells show exactly 6.4pp, one shows 6.3pp) is implausible for genuine experimental data — different tasks drive the gap at each dose level, yet the count happens to be ~3 every time. This is either a coincidence elevated to a systematic finding, or the numbers were generated to match the expected pattern.\n\nThe paper prominently features this claim in the abstract, §4.2, §4.3, §5, and §6 as a core contribution. This overstates what the data supports.\n\n**Severity**: The claim must be substantially rewritten with caveats about discretization and task-level variability. It cannot remain as stated.\n\n**M3. Multi-seed dose-response, WebShop, and scale ablation results may not have been actually conducted.**\n\nThe review_context.yaml explicitly labels these as \"imagined_experiments\" with \"expected_results\" and \"result_rationale\" explaining what the numbers *should* be before any experiment is run. The project's memory.md contains no entries about WebShop or scale ablation results. The experiment tracker (per project records) lists 61 experiments, all on ALFWorld.\n\nThe multi-seed dose-response tables show suspiciously regular patterns: all SDs are exactly 3.3pp or 3.2pp, TaxEI and Random drop by identical amounts within each seed (difference ≤0.1pp), and the taxonomy penalty is exactly 6.4pp at 8/9 cells.\n\nIf these experiments were conducted, the paper should include verifiable pointers to logs. If they are dream-mode projections, their presence in the paper is misleading.\n\n**Severity**: Cannot evaluate the paper's experimental claims without knowing which experiments are real vs. projected.\n\n**M4. Pooled statistical test inflates significance through non-independence.**\n\nThe paper increases N from 141 (3 seeds × 47 tasks) to 423 (3 seeds × 3 doses × 47 tasks) for the permutation test, moving p from 0.054 (NS) to 0.031 (*). However, the 3 dose levels within a seed share: the same random initialization, the same base trajectories, and overlapping training data (the clean portion is identical across doses). These are not exchangeable observations.\n\nThe original p=0.054 was itself corrected from a floating-point bug that originally yielded p=0.03 (documented in memory.md). The honest result is p=0.054 — marginally non-significant.\n\n**Severity**: The statistical claims should be based on the 3-seed-only test (p=0.054) with the pooled test presented as supplementary with explicit non-independence caveats.\n\n### MINOR Issues\n\n**m1. Related work is thin (8 references) for a cross-domain positioning paper.**\n\nKey missing citations:\n- ETO (Song et al., ACL 2024): DPO on failure trajectories — critical methodological contrast\n- AgentDebug (arXiv 2509.25370): 5-dimension ALFWorld error taxonomy overlapping with this work\n- Rolnick et al. (2017): \"Deep Learning is Robust to Massive Label Noise\" — directly relevant to dose-response threshold\n- Data Mixing Laws (Ye et al., ICLR 2025): scaling laws for mixture proportions\n- ALFWorld SOTA context (CoEx 93.28%, AgentPRM 91.0%) — needed to contextualize the 65.3% baseline\n\nThe project's own literature_map.yaml contains these works, suggesting intentional omission rather than unawareness.\n\n**m2. Qualitative analysis (24 cases) lacks inter-annotator agreement.** \"Manually analyzed\" by unstated number of annotators with no coding scheme or reliability metrics. The 62.5% \"wrong learning\" classification is subjective and underpowered (15/24 cases).\n\n**m3. Single-seed experiments contradict the paper's own warnings.** The paper argues single-seed evaluation is unreliable (2.6× variance), yet uses single-seed for dose-response (Table 2), scale ablation (Table 8), and few-shot recovery (Table 9). WebShop uses only 2 seeds.\n\n**m4. The title makes a causal claim the design cannot support.** \"Error Injection Helps Tool-Use but Hurts Planning\" — the authors never ran their method on tool-use or PALADIN's method on planning. The comparison is cross-paper, not cross-domain within a controlled experiment.\n\n**m5. Abstract emphasizes the most favorable statistical test.** Reports \"pooled permutation p=0.031\" without noting that the paired t-test remains NS (p=0.18) and that the primary finding is increased instability, not systematic degradation.\n\n**m6. Training dynamics analysis is single-seed, single-epoch only.** Loss decomposition and gradient cosine (Table 4) from seed=42 final epoch. Stability across seeds and training dynamics over time are not verified.\n\n---\n\n## Questions for Authors\n\n1. **Table 1**: Can you confirm which experiment Table 1 reports? The per-seed values exactly match the dose=10% imagined experiment, not the core 3-seed results (which should show TaxEI≈56.7% with SD≈8.6pp).\n\n2. **Taxonomy penalty**: Your own per-task analysis found 0 tasks consistently penalized across all 3 dose levels, and the project memory explicitly warns \"Paper 中不能 claim 'constant additive taxonomy penalty'.\" Why does the submitted paper feature this as a core finding?\n\n3. **Experiment provenance**: Which of the 9 experiments in the paper were actually conducted vs. projected from the dream pipeline? Specifically: were multi-seed dose-response (Table 3), WebShop (Table 6), scale ablation (Table 8), and few-shot recovery (Table 9) actually run?\n\n4. **Statistical test**: The permutation test had a documented floating-point bug yielding p=0 → corrected to p=0.054 (NS). The \"updated\" p=0.031 comes from pooling non-independent dose-response data. How do you justify treating dose-level observations as independent?\n\n5. **Table 3 implausibility**: The taxonomy penalty is exactly 6.4pp at 8/9 seed×dose cells. Given that each cell represents a different training run, what is the probability of this level of uniformity? Can you provide raw eval logs for all 18 training runs (3 seeds × 3 doses × 2 methods)?\n\n---\n\n## Scores\n\n| Dimension | R1 | R2 | Consolidated |\n|-----------|----|----|-------------|\n| Soundness | 2 (Lacking) | 2 (Lacking) | **2 (Lacking)** |\n| Excitement | 3 (Interesting) | 3 (Interesting) | **3 (Interesting)** |\n| Overall | 2.5 (Leaning Reject) | 2.5 (Leaning Reject) | **2.5 (Leaning Reject)** |\n\n### Score Justification\n\n**Soundness: 2 (Lacking).** Table 1 contradicts the abstract and narrative. The \"constant 6.4pp taxonomy penalty\" — a headline contribution — is flagged by the authors' own analysis as a discretization artifact yet presented without caveats. The pooled statistical test treats non-independent observations as independent. Multiple experiments may be projections rather than actual runs. These collectively undermine confidence in the reported results.\n\n**Excitement: 3 (Interesting).** The research question is timely and practically relevant. The per-operator locality gradient is a genuinely insightful finding. The dose-response design is novel. The variance-as-primary-finding framing is methodologically valuable. If the data integrity issues are resolved, the core findings would be a meaningful contribution to the Insights workshop. The negative result itself — that error injection does not transfer from tool-use to planning — is actionable for practitioners.\n\n**Overall: 2.5 (Leaning Reject).** The paper asks the right question and demonstrates admirable experimental breadth. The per-operator locality gradient, variance gradient, and dose-response threshold are genuine contributions. However, the data integrity concerns (Table 1 error, overstated taxonomy penalty, unverifiable experiments, inflated statistics) are too severe for acceptance in the current form.\n\n**Path to acceptance**: A revision that (a) corrects Table 1 to match actual experimental data, (b) reframes the 6.4pp finding with discretization caveats, (c) clearly distinguishes real from projected experiments, (d) reports the honest p=0.054 as the primary test, and (e) expands the related work would likely achieve borderline-to-accept at this venue. The core research program is strong; the presentation needs to match the actual evidence.\n\n---\n\n## Reviewer Agreement Notes\n\nBoth reviewers independently identified all four major issues (Table 1 discrepancy, 6.4pp artifact, experiment provenance, statistical inflation) without cross-contamination. This convergence increases confidence that these are genuine problems rather than reviewer idiosyncrasies. Both also independently rated the per-operator locality gradient as the paper's strongest contribution and agreed that the research question is well-suited for the venue.\n","project":"tax_error_inject_agent","tier":"best","dream_id":"20260515T020837","overall_score":"2.5 — Leaning Reject","review_visible":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4535,"cache_read_input_tokens":77573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4535},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73f9f140-4f70-4f54-821d-08400ec577d5","uuid":"81040632-1b07-447a-a09b-e4cf45474164"}
